{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-37649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-37770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+3z=7 \\\\ 0x+y+2z=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3z=7 \\\\ y+2z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+3z=7\\,⇒\\,x=7-3z\n$$\n\nand from the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\ny+2z=-3\\,⇒\\,y=-3-2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3z \\\\ y=-3-2z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7-3z \\\\ -3-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-37774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3-3z \\\\ 7-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7+3z \\\\ -3+2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7+3z \\\\ 3-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7-3z \\\\ -3-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-37774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}7-3z \\\\ -3-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-131484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-131484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+7y-8z=0 \\\\ 0x+y-z=-7 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+7y-8z=0 \\\\ y-z=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-z=-7\\,⇒\\,y=z-7\n$$\n\nand from the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx+7(z-7)-8z=0\\,⇒\\,x=z+49.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=z+49 \\\\ y=z-7 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}z+49 \\\\ z-7 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-131484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-131484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-131484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}z+49 \\\\ 7-z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}z+49 \\\\ z-7 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}z+7 \\\\ z-7 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}z-49 \\\\ z+7 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}z-7 \\\\ z+7 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-131484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}z+49 \\\\ z-7 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-20967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-20967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+2z=-2 \\\\ 0x+y-3z=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2z=-2 \\\\ y-3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3z=3\\,⇒\\,y=3+3z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand from the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2z=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2-2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-2z \\\\ y=3+3z \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2-2z \\\\ 3+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-20967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-20967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-20967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-20967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 7 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+7z=-9 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx-2y+7z=-9\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=-9+2y-7z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-9+2y-7z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9+2y-7z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\be