0273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-131498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x+5y+0z=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n-x+5y=3\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=5y-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5y-3 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5y-3 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-131498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-131498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacadem