277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-4z=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx+2y-4z=3\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=3-2y+4z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2y+4z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-2y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-73914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2-3y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3+2y-4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3-2y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3-4y+2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3-2y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-10{x}_{3}=40 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 20 & -10 & 40 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 20 & -10 & 40 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -5 & 20 & -10 & 40 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-73918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 34\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-6z=8 \\\\ 0x-y-12z=16 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=34,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a67639f987b020273f05845ac1ef3068df103fba9f2e8702277c9a22275"} {"question" "q-73958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f"} {"question" "q-73958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "020b8a6